---
description: Every balance-holding program ships tests that fail if an invariant stops holding.
globs: "**/{tests,programs}/**/*.{rs,ts}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

- If a program holds a balance, it has a test for invariant 1 (no arbitrary treasury send) and rounding direction.
- Token-2022 NonTransferable: MintTo/Burn from the PDA treasury must pass; a PDA-signed transfer must fail at Token-2022; TransferFeeConfig on that mint must fail. See `tests/token2022.ts`.
- A test must fail if the invariant it names stops holding. Do not assert logs or "did not panic" as a substitute.
- Cross-program numbers that appear in more than one crate belong in a seam test against `transmuter-constants`.
- CU / finalize: `tests/finalize_cu.ts` is a mock-DEX stand-in. Re-measure on the real DEX before treating `convertTreasury` as closed.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
expect(tx).to.not.equal(null);

// ✅ GOOD
expect(acc.amount).to.equal(BigInt(MINT_AMOUNT / 2));
```
